stemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22bug%20%F0%9F%90%9B%22) Programming errors, that need preferential fixing [pid1](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22pid1%22)\n\n## Description\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\nopened [on Aug 5, 2015on Aug 6, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issue-99339363)\n\nContributor\n\nIssue body actions\n\nCurrently, `Type=dbus` is unsuitable for things like notification daemons because `BusName=` is expected to appear on the system bus, but `org.freedesktop.Notification` is meant for the session bus.\n\n## Activity\n\n### poettering commented on Aug 6, 2015on Aug 6, 2015\n\n[![@poettering](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2130732?u=8b2c8c8295327817db30aa12b358ece41decd075&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/poettering)\n\n[poettering](https://github.com/poettering)\n\n[on Aug 6, 2015on Aug 6, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-128272985)\n\nMember\n\nMore actions\n\nHmm? no... Type=dbus services with BusName= set should watch the user bus for the systemd user instance and the session bus for the systemd system instance. Are you saying that that's not what you are seeing?\n\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2130732?s=64&u=8b2c8c8295327817db30aa12b358ece41decd075&v=4)poettering](https://github.com/poettering)\n\nadded\n\n[pid1](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22pid1%22)\n\n[needs-reporter-feedback ❓There's an unanswered question, the reporter needs to answer](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22needs-reporter-feedback%20%E2%9D%93%22) There's an unanswered question, the reporter needs to answer\n\n[on Aug 6, 2015on Aug 6, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#event-375005122)\n\n### mathstuf commented on Aug 6, 2015on Aug 6, 2015\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Aug 6, 2015on Aug 6, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-128354188)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\n[#891](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/891) would help debugging this ;) . I did have to change a user service from dbus to simple due to a timeout though. I'll try and switch it back tonight. Is a dbus-1/…/foo.service file required for it to work at all? Would also be good for the docs and error message if so.\n\n### mathstuf commented on Aug 7, 2015on Aug 7, 2015\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Aug 7, 2015on Aug 7, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-128860808)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\nUsing `Type=dbus` and `BusName=org.freedesktop.Notifications`:\n\n```\n% qdbus\n:1.19\n org.gtk.vfs.Metadata\n:1.2\n im.pidgin.purple.PurpleService\n:1.3\n:1.4\n org.PulseAudio1\n org.freedesktop.ReserveDevice1.Audio0\n org.pulseaudio.Server\n:1.41\n org.gtk.Private.UDisks2VolumeMonitor\n:1.43\n:1.6\n org.gtk.vfs.Daemon\n:1.8\n org.a11y.Bus\n:1.92\n:1.93\n:1.96\n org.freedesktop.Notifications\n:1.97\norg.freedesktop.DBus\n```\n\nLog:\n\n```\nAug 07 19:44:47 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: Stopping Dunst notification daemon...\nAug 07 19:44:47 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: Stopped Dunst notification daemon.\nAug 07 19:44:47 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: Starting Dunst notification daemon...\nAug 07 19:46:17 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: dunst.service: Start operation timed out. Terminating.\nAug 07 19:46:17 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: Failed to start Dunst notification daemon.\nAug 07 19:46:17 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: dunst.service: Unit entered failed state.\nAug 07 19:46:17 bronto-burt systemd[6093]: dunst.service: Failed with result 'timeout'.\n```\n\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/623857?s=64&u=692f1c8df283ff6902fda1cb2deaa2d49fd53c4a&v=4)dvdhrm](https://github.com/dvdhrm)\n\nadded\n\n[bug 🐛Programming errors, that need preferential fixing](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22bug%20%F0%9F%90%9B%22) Programming errors, that need preferential fixing\n\nand removed\n\n[needs-reporter-feedback ❓There's an unanswered question, the reporter needs to answer](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22needs-reporter-feedback%20%E2%9D%93%22) There's an unanswered question, the reporter needs to answer\n\n[on Sep 5, 2015on Sep 5, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#event-401947980)\n\n### mathstuf commented on Sep 12, 2015on Sep 12, 2015\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Sep 12, 2015on Sep 12, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-139780500)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\nTried again with a better `dbus-1` service file:\n\n`.local/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.Notifications.service`:\n\n```\n[D-BUS Service]\nName=org.freedesktop.Notifications\nExec=/usr/bin/dunst\nSystemdService=dunst.service\n```\n\n`.local/share/systemd/user/dunst.service`:\n\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=Dunst notification daemon\nRequires=xorg.target\nAfter=xorg.target\n\n[Service]\nType=dbus\nBusName=org.freedesktop.Notifications\nExecStart=/usr/bin/dunst\n```\n\n### mathstuf commented on Sep 12, 2015on Sep 12, 2015\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Sep 12, 2015on Sep 12, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-139781279)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\nOh, same result with these units: a timeout.\n\n### chmorgan commented on Sep 30, 2015on Sep 30, 2015\n\n[![@chmorgan](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1211904?u=11c43d7fcf9660b867d1d5a221bd7c7c7e85d52e&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/chmorgan)\n\n[chmorgan](https://github.com/chmorgan)\n\n[on Sep 30, 2015on Sep 30, 2015](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-144518245)\n\nContributor\n\nMore actions\n\nI'm seeing the same here with systemd 219, that Type=dbus isn't working correctly with user services.\n\n### kamathba commented on Jun 20, 2016on Jun 20, 2016\n\n[![@kamathba](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2832151?u=d7f92abf3b1ae32ce319313f38e410fbaf0f82d8&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/kamathba)\n\n[kamathba](https://github.com/kamathba)\n\n[on Jun 20, 2016on Jun 20, 2016](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-227311477)\n\nLast edited by kamathba\n\nMore actions\n\nSame problem with systemd 222, switching it to type notify and using sd\\_notify worked.\n\n### smcv commented on Apr 5, 2017on Apr 5, 2017\n\n[![@smcv](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1561141?u=daeb9f79b5ea25e2a8dd236af718393f95e153c3&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/smcv)\n\n[smcv](https://github.com/smcv)\n\n[on Apr 5, 2017on Apr 5, 2017](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-291822370)\n\nLast edited by smcv\n\nContributor\n\nMore actions\n\n`Type=dbus` works fine for user-services that are D-Bus session services on Debian testing/unstable with the `dbus-user-session` package installed, so I think this is some configuration issue in whatever OS you're using. `gnome-terminal-server`, `xdg-desktop-portal`, `flatpak-session-helper`, `evince`, `mpDris2` are among the user-services for which it definitely works for me.\n\nThis is not going to work if `systemd --user` can't or doesn't connect to your D-Bus session bus (aka user bus). I don't see `org.freedesktop.systemd` in [the list of owned names above](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-128860808), which suggests that systemd has not succesfully connected to that bus; if it hasn't connected, then it is clearly not going to notice that dunst has claimed its bus name.\n\nHow, exactly, are you running `dbus-daemon --session`? On which OS distribution? What is your `$DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS`?\n\nIf you are using the same setup as Debian with the `dbus-user-session` package, Fedora and Arch Linux, then you should have a socket `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus` with socket activation from `dbus.socket`, which starts `dbus.service` on connection attempts; and `systemd --user` should be connecting to that socket and requesting the `org.freedesktop.systemd` name.\n\n> Type=dbus services with BusName= set should watch the user bus for the systemd user instance and the session bus for the systemd system instance.\n\nI assume that was meant to say: should watch the user bus (aka session bus, `dbus-daemon --session`) for the systemd user instance (`systemd --user`), and the **system** bus (`dbus-daemon --system`) for the systemd system instance (pid 1).\n\n### mathstuf commented on Apr 5, 2017on Apr 5, 2017\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Apr 5, 2017on Apr 5, 2017](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-291879638)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\nHere is my `dbus.service`:\n\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=D-Bus System Message Bus\nWants=environment.target\nAfter=environment.target\nAfter=dbus-env.service\nRequires=dbus.socket\n\n[Service]\nExecStart=/usr/bin/dbus-daemon --session --address=systemd: --nofork --nopidfile --systemd-activation\nExecReload=/usr/bin/dbus-send --session --print-reply --type=method_call --dest=org.freedesktop.DBus / org.freedesktop.DBus.ReloadConfig\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=x11-standard.target\nAlso=dbus.socket\n```\n\n`dbus-env.service`:\n\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=DBus Environment\nWants=environment.target\nBefore=environment.target\nBindsTo=dbus.service\n\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nRemainAfterExit=yes\nExecStart=/usr/bin/systemctl --user set-environment DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=%t/dbus/user_bus_socket\nExecStop=/usr/bin/systemctl --user unset-environment DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=environment.target\n```\n\n`dbus.socket`:\n\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=D-Bus System Message Bus Socket\nBindsTo=dbus.service\n\n[Socket]\nListenStream=%t/dbus/user_bus_socket\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=x11-standard.target\n```\n\n### smcv commented on Apr 11, 2017on Apr 11, 2017\n\n[![@smcv](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1561141?u=daeb9f79b5ea25e2a8dd236af718393f95e153c3&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/smcv)\n\n[smcv](https://github.com/smcv)\n\n[on Apr 11, 2017on Apr 11, 2017](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-293227973)\n\nContributor\n\nMore actions\n\n> Here is my `dbus.service`\n\nLet me guess, you got that from [https://github.com/sofar/user-session-units](https://github.com/sofar/user-session-units)? Those units are not a product of either the systemd maintainers or the dbus maintainers, although some of them acted as a useful prototype for what was later merged into dbus.\n\ndbus 1.10 or later, built with `--enable-user-session`, obsoletes those units by providing its own. These use the socket that systemd assumes, namely `%t/bus`.\n\n### mathstuf commented on Apr 11, 2017on Apr 11, 2017\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[mathstuf](https://github.com/mathstuf)\n\n[on Apr 11, 2017on Apr 11, 2017](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892#issuecomment-293230246)\n\nContributorAuthor\n\nMore actions\n\nNo, I had written many of these up before many user units got written (2009 or 2010 IIRC?), but only started using them in 2012 or so. I use these rather than upstream because I do the `environment.target` setup for managing environment variables and to ensure they are all set before services which may need them start up (it'd be nice if systemd would have standard targets for things like that so that in the user session services can start with a full environment).\n\nSo if I use `%t/bus` things should work? Isn't that a bug? I'll look in more detail what is different from upstream's units.\n\n### 5 remaining items\n\nLoad more\n\nLoading\n\n[Sign up for free](https://github.com/signup?return_to=https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892)**to join this conversation on GitHub.** Already have an account? [Sign in to comment](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/892)\n\n## Metadata\n\n## Metadata\n\n### Assignees\n\nNo one assigned\n\n### Labels\n\n[bug 🐛Programming errors, that need preferential fixing](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22bug%20%F0%9F%90%9B%22) Programming errors, that need preferential fixing [pid1](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22pid1%22)\n\n### Type\n\nNo type\n\n### Projects\n\nNo projects\n\n### Milestone\n\nNo milestone\n\n### Relationships\n\nNone yet\n\n### Development\n\nNo branches or pull requests\n\n### Participants\n\n[![@mathstuf](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97253?s=64&v=4)](https://github.com/mathstuf)[![@dvdhrm](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/623857?s=64&u=692f1c8df283ff6902fda1cb2deaa2d49fd53c4a&v=4)](https://github.com/dvdhrm)[![@chmorgan](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1211904?s=64&u=11c43d7fcf9660b867d1d5a221bd7c7c7e85d52e&v=4)](https://github.com/chmorgan)[![@smcv](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1561141?s=64&u=daeb9f79b5ea25e2a8dd236af718393f95e153c3&v=4)](https://github.com/smcv)[![@sofar](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1880041?s=64&u=58ee185e88159bd1e2dfa4dc55abe36e58024f4c&v=4)](https://github.com/sofar)\n\n+2\n\n## Issue actions\n\n- ![](https://github.githubassets.com/assets/github-copilot-app-light-15ad5534265eeacd.svg)Open in GitHub Copilot app