n them into a linefeed literal. In your case this would look something like this:\n\n```\nJWT_PUB_KEY=\"-----BEGIN FOO BAR KEY-----\\n\\\nMIIBgjAcBgoqhkiG9w0BDAEDMA4ECKZesfWLQOiDAgID6ASCAWBu7izm8N4V\\n\\\n2puRO/Mdt+Y8ceywxiC0cE57nrbmvaTSvBwTg9b/xyd8YC6QK7lrhC9Njgp/\\n\\\n...\\n\\\n-----END FOO BAR KEY-----\"\n```\n\n[Share](https://stackoverflow.com/a/38760831)\n\nShare a link to this answer\n\nCopy link [CC BY-SA 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ \"The current license for this post: CC BY-SA 3.0\")\n\nShort permalink to this answer\n\n[Improve this answer](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/38760831/edit \"\")\n\nFollow\n\n\n\nFollow this answer to receive notifications\n\nanswered Aug 4, 2016 at 7:18\n\n[![Vality's user avatar](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/1227f90127f0f7b8678a8c13261f48b4?s=64&d=identicon&r=PG)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3323096/vality)\n\n[Vality](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3323096/vality)\n\n6,59033 gold badges3131 silver badges4848 bronze badges\n\n## 6 Comments\n\nAdd a comment\n\n[![](https://i.sstatic.net/CREfl.png?s=64)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon)\n\nallan.simon\n\n[allan.simon](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon) [Over a year ago](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35909874/systemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant#comment64905363_38760831)\n\nlet me test that again, I think I've tested that combination, because I ended up with \\`\\\\\\n\\` but it's been a long time so I may have overlooked\n\n2016-08-04T12:18:47.973Z+00:00\n\n0\n\nReply\n\n- Copy link\n\n[![](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/06f202577dda407e88153c91f0a3354d?s=48&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3504681/daniel-kravetz-malabud)\n\nDaniel Kravetz Malabud\n\n[Daniel Kravetz Malabud](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3504681/daniel-kravetz-malabud) [Over a year ago](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35909874/systemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant#comment64961982_38760831)\n\n\\\\\\n would result in parsing the character '\\\\' and parsing the character 'n' instead of the newline character '\\\\n'\n\n2016-08-05T18:40:24.5Z+00:00\n\n0\n\nReply\n\n- Copy link\n\n[![](https://i.sstatic.net/CREfl.png?s=64)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon)\n\nallan.simon\n\n[allan.simon](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon) [Over a year ago](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35909874/systemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant#comment65627968_38760831)\n\n@Vality, actually it doesn't work, when I do that, and then I print in python I got the whole variable in one line\n\n2016-08-25T09:44:49.723Z+00:00\n\n1\n\nReply\n\n- Copy link\n\n[![](https://i.sstatic.net/CREfl.png?s=64)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon)\n\nallan.simon\n\n[allan.simon](https://stackoverflow.com/users/1185460/allan-simon) [Over a year ago](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35909874/systemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant#comment80983418_38760831)\n\nfor my very specific case, actually I solved this now in a better way by using the public key in ssh format, which is a one-liner, so no problem.\n\n2017-10-30T15:04:17.55Z+00:00\n\n0\n\nReply\n\n- Copy link\n\n[![](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ef53a40bb25a507097634d2e869e17c7?s=48&d=identicon&r=PG)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/310121/erik-b)\n\nErik B\n\n[Erik B](https://stackoverflow.com/users/310121/erik-b) [Over a year ago](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35909874/systemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant#comment111228676_38760831)\n\n@allan.simon Why did you accept this answer if it doesn't work?\n\n2020-07-14T15:19:48.793Z+00:00\n\n3\n\nReply\n\n- Copy link\n\nAdd a comment\n\nThis answer is useful\n\n0\n\nThis answer is not useful\n\nSave this answer.\n\nLoading when this answer was accepted…\n\n[Timeline](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/38795910/timeline)\n\nShow activity on this post.\n\nYou shouldn't have to interpret (parse?) the newline characters on your end, that should all happen automatically, [as explained here](https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/systemd.service.html) , meaning that adding '\\\\n' at the end of each line should do the trick.\n\n[Share](https://stackoverflow.com/a/38795910)\n\nShare a link to this answer\n\nCopy link [CC BY-SA 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ \"The current license for this post: CC BY-SA 3.0\")\n\nShort permalink to this answer\n\n[Improve this answer](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/38795910/edit \"\")\n\nFollow\n\n\n\nFollow this answer to receive notifications\n\nanswered Aug 5, 2016 at 18:43\n\n[![Daniel Kravetz Malabud's user avatar](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/06f202577dda407e88153c91f0a3354d?s=64&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3504681/daniel-kravetz-malabud)\n\n[Daniel Kravetz Malabud](https://stackoverflow.com/users/3504681/daniel-kravetz-malabud)\n\n78333 silver badges1212 bronze badges\n\n## Comments\n\nAdd a comment\n\nThis answer is useful\n\n0\n\nThis answer is not useful\n\nSave this answer.\n\nLoading when this answer was accepted…\n\n[Timeline](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/75026866/timeline)\n\nShow activity on this post.\n\nDepending on your systemd version, you cannot use the above answers. (you can check the version by `systemctl --version`.) Actually any versions before [this PR](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/pull/8471) was merged should not be able to use multiline environment variables. For example, Amazon Linux 2 seems to use systemd v219, which was released on 2015/02.\n\nManually upgrading systemd is usually not recommended ( [ref](https://askubuntu.com/a/627203)), so there are not many things you can do about this issue.\n\nAs a workaround, I encoded the value in base64 and decoded it in the application.\n\n```bash\nCopy\n# encode\n# you need -w 0 option to wrap newlines\necho \"YOUR_MULTILINE_VARIABLE\" | base64 -w 0\n```\n\n[Share](https://stackoverflow.com/a/75026866)\n\nShare a link to this answer\n\nCopy link [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ \"The current license for this post: CC BY-SA 4.0\")\n\nShort permalink to this answer\n\n[Improve this answer](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/75026866/edit \"\")\n\nFollow\n\n\n\nFollow this answer to receive notifications\n\n[edited Jan 6, 2023 at 5:25](https://stackoverflow.com/posts/75026866/revisions \"show all edits to this post\")\n\nanswered Jan 6, 2023 at 4:14\n\n[![tmokmss's user avatar](https://i.sstatic.net/GQgu9.jpg?s=64)](https://stackoverflow.com/users/18550269/tmokmss)\n\n[tmokmss](https://stackoverflow.com/users/18550269/tmokmss)\n\n55811 gold badge44 silver badges1111 bronze badges\n\n## Comments\n\nAdd a comment\n\n## Your Answer\n\n**Reminder:** Answers generated by AI tools are not allowed due to Stack Overflow's [artificial intelligence policy](https://stackoverflow.com/help/gen-ai-policy)\n\nDraft saved\n\nDraft discarded\n\n### Sign up or [log in](https://stackoverflow.com/users/login?ssrc=question_page&returnurl=https%3a%2f%2fstackoverflow.com%2fquestions%2f35909874%2fsystemd-multiline-variable-in-environmentfile-where-new-line-is-significant%23new-answer)\n\nSign up using Google\n\n\nSign up using Email and Password\n\n\nSubmit\n\n### Post as a guest\n\nName\n\nEmail\n\nRequired, but never shown\n\nPost Your Answer\n\nDiscard\n\n\nBy clicking “Post Your Answer”, you agree to our [terms of service](https://stackoverflow.com/legal/terms-of-service/public) and acknowledge you have read our [privacy policy](https://stackoverflow.com/legal/privacy-policy).\n\n\nStart asking to get answers\n\nFind the answer to your question by asking.\n\n[Ask question](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/ask)\n\nExplore related questions\n\n- [systemd](https://stackoverflow.com/questions